# Test coverage every time

Do not ship a behavior change without automated coverage in the same change. If you add or change logic, add or update a test. Do not finish with “tests later”.

This repo runs Vitest with a single root `vitest.config.ts` (`projects` for `packages/shared`, `apps/api`, `apps/web`) and `all: true` coverage held at **100% lines, branches, functions and statements**. Untested code fails `pnpm coverage`, so new code arrives with its test or it does not arrive.

```
# ❌ BAD — new helper, no test
src/lib/period-bounds.ts

# ✅ GOOD — helper plus colocated test
src/lib/period-bounds.ts
src/lib/period-bounds.test.ts
```

- Colocate `foo.test.ts` next to `foo.ts` (same folder), or `index.test.ts` beside `index.ts` in a module folder. React components use `index.test.tsx`.
- Web components are tested with React Testing Library plus `@testing-library/user-event`, rendered through `renderWithProviders` from `@/test/render`. Query by role and label, not by class or test id, unless there is nothing else.
- API tests use `createTestDb` / `openTestDb` (PGlite) and `withUser` for RLS, like `projects.filters.check`-era code now does in `*.test.ts`.
- Prefer extracting logic (pure functions, SQL filters, routers, schemas, parsers) out of UI so it can be asserted directly, but a branch that only exists in a component still needs a component test.
- Changing covered behavior means **updating the test**, not deleting assertions.
- Keep a Better Auth callback a named exported function instead of an inline arrow; the 100% function threshold needs a handle on it.
- Third-party primitives copied in verbatim (`src/components/ui/*.tsx` from shadcn, `Grainient`) are excluded in `vitest.config.ts`. Add a new one to that list rather than writing a test for code you did not write.
- Run `pnpm test` while iterating and `pnpm coverage` before declaring done.

**Out of scope** (no new test file): copy-only i18n catalog edits, comments, Cursor rules, docs, and CSS with no behavior change. Still run existing tests if those files are already covered (e.g. `pnpm --filter web check:i18n`).
